$ krowk help uploads --format human
stdout:
krowk artifacts — Create, list, show, attach, delete or claim artifacts

An artifact is a file published to a link. `krowk push` and `krowk claim`
are the short forms of `create` and `claim`; `uploads` is an older name.

Commands (krowk artifacts …)
  create <file...> [flags]    Upload files: the long form of `krowk push`
  list [flags]                List artifacts, newest first: a run's, or the
                              workspace's
  show <artifact>             Read one artifact back
  attach <art> --run <run>    Put an artifact under a run afterwards
  delete <art> [token]        Take an artifact down — immediate, cannot be
                              undone
  claim <art> <token> [--run]
                              The long form of `krowk claim`

Global flags: --workspace --dev --format --json --quiet --jq — see `help flags`
exit: 0

